It is considered good practice to add examples in here to demonstrate the
functionality of your OOT module. Python scripts, GRC flow graphs or other
code can go here.
drm_fac_runtime_test.grc is a minimal GNU Radio Companion runtime check. It
generates three DRM Fast Access Channel (FAC) frames and writes 216 binary
output bytes to drm_fac_output.bin.

drm_live_soundcard.grc continuously encodes a low-level 1 kHz programme tone
through the full DRM transmitter and emits a real 48 kHz, 7 kHz-IF baseband
waveform through the default sound-card sink. Route it to a virtual audio cable
or line output and keep speaker volume low. Replace the Signal Source with an
Audio Source block to use a microphone or loopback input.
